   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## A generated model onto the real one\n\nAn image-to-3D workflow gives a model that sits anywhere in space. **kubakub align 3d model** lays it onto the real model of the building, so it opens in Blender or Houdini in the right place, at the right size.\n\n**Queue as it is:** nothing is connected, so a sample runs (the sample facade as the template, and the same building turned, moved, shrunk and a quarter too deep). The report says what was wrong and what was done.\n\n**With your own:** connect the MESH of an image-to-3D node to **model** (or put a .glb path in `model_file`) and the path of your real model in `template_file` (export it as .glb from Blender or Houdini). `scale` = *per axis* corrects a misread depth or height. The aligned file is written to output/3d.\n"
   ]
  }
